# Comparing the odd-exponent E.2.2 models with the full FF component catalogue

Suzuki and PSU₃ are absent from every central component carrier in B.4.2's
eleven alternatives. PSL₂, PSL₃ and Sp₄ match exactly their corresponding
families, with the same defining-field cardinality. The proofs retain both
small derived endpoints, the alternating quotients of central covers, and
the binary linear exceptions until their actual orders exclude them.

Suzuki has three-free order, whereas every catalogue entry has order
divisible by three. For the other families, the two-part of the order and
elementary two-rank distinguish the actual carriers. The unitary field
parameter is the fixed-field order; its matrix field has square cardinality.
The canonical SL₃/PSL₃ projection at odd exponent and the nonbinary
Sp₄′/Sp₄ inclusion preserve every subgroup image. The faithful section-image
comparisons use the parent's central-kernel theorem and retain that kernel.

These are concrete group comparisons. The source B.4.2/B.5.1 case split,
module deductions and exchanged-component assembly belong to their callers.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), printed
pp.86--87, 99--100, 215--216 and the application on p.1152.
-/
